{
  "title": "Lunch Hour",
  "logline": "Michael's mandatory \"Team Lunch Efficiency\" initiative runs into Pam's canceled lunch with Roy, Dwight's title scheming, and Ryan's website pitch.",
  "outline": "A: Michael bans desk lunches and forces a \"family lunch\" in the conference room, wanting to be loved. B: Roy cancels on Pam; Jim eats with her in the parking lot (Pam/Jim), while Dwight tries to become the lunch enforcer. C: Ryan pitches a website to David on the phone; Andy tries too hard. Order: cold, A, B, C, A, B, A, C, B, A, tag",
  "theme": "Who do you eat lunch with: being chosen.",
  "storySoFar": "Michael's dinner with Jan was canceled earlier; the office gave him a warm moment. Ryan is his reluctant protege and this week pitched a website to David Wallace, who said he'd look at it. Dwight campaigns for Assistant Regional Manager; owes beet refunds; Jim holds one real beet. Pam keeps Jim's lamp on; Roy canceled lunch on her again and Jim sat with her in the parking lot, nothing said. Andy tried too hard to be liked and got iced out of the family lunch. Michael's family lunch ended with him eating alone, then the office joining him.",
  "extras": [],
